diff --git a/docs/deployment.md b/docs/deployment.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..78e94c8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# Deploying to one server
+
+The included [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org/) configuration runs Fizzy on a
+single Linux server. The server needs SSH access and Docker; the computer you
+deploy from needs Docker and the repository's Ruby dependencies. Kamal runs the
+web server and Solid Queue workers in one app container and terminates HTTPS
+with `kamal-proxy`.
+
+Production uses SQLite and local file storage. The `fizzy_storage` Docker volume
+is mounted at `/rails/storage`, so the databases and uploaded files survive app
+container replacements.
+
+## Configure
+
+1. Point a DNS record at the server and allow inbound traffic on ports 80 and
+   443. In [`config/deploy.yml`](../config/deploy.yml),
+   replace `fizzy.example.com` at the top with that DNS name. Update the sender
+   and the `SMTP_*` values for your mail server too. The default configuration
+   expects authenticated SMTP with STARTTLS on port 587.
+
+   If the server is ARM64 rather than AMD64, also change `builder.arch` to
+   `arm64`.
+
+2. Store the deployment secrets in the local, gitignored files used by
+   [`.kamal/secrets`](../.kamal/secrets):
+
+   ```sh
+   umask 077
+   bin/rails secret > .kamal/secret_key_base
+   printf '%s' 'your-smtp-username' > .kamal/smtp_username
+   printf '%s' 'your-smtp-password' > .kamal/smtp_password
+   ```
+
+   Keep `secret_key_base` unchanged after the first deploy. Changing it signs
+   everyone out and invalidates existing signed links. You can edit
+   `.kamal/secrets` to load these values from a password manager instead.
+   The local files are excluded from both Git and Docker image builds.
+
+3. Make sure you can connect to the server as `root` over SSH, then deploy:
+
+   ```sh
+   bin/kamal setup
+   ```
+
+Kamal will build the image, install and start `kamal-proxy`, prepare all four
+SQLite databases, and start Fizzy at `https://your-host`. Later releases use:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+Useful commands include `bin/kamal console`, `bin/kamal shell`, and
+`bin/kamal logs`.
+
+## Backups
+
+The Docker volume survives deployments but is not a backup. Back up
+`fizzy_storage` regularly; it contains both the SQLite databases and uploaded
+files. Stop writes or use SQLite's backup tooling when copying a live database.
